--- body ---
## Context

Today every selected credential is exported into the environment of every
non-interactive bash, by `BASH_ENV` -> `scripts/bash-env.sh`. That design was
deliberate and was an improvement: before it, keys were inlined in argv, and on
2026-04-30 a single `ps -ef` surfaced a dozen of them in plaintext and forced a
full rotation. Moving them out of argv fixed that. It did not fix residency.

What residency costs, measured rather than assumed:

- Six live values printed to stderr by a plain `bash -x` (0939, fixed for the
  trace channel only).
- The same six readable in `/proc/<pid>/environ` of every child, and inherited
  by any project script the agent runs, including from a cloned repo.
- Two live keys leaked on 2026-07-27 when a test's stub child was re-injected
  with the real credential over an injected fixture.
- 0360: a project's `KEYS=` REPLACES the harness one rather than composing, so a
  harness-selected credential is silently absent from a project cwd. "A miss is
  a silent auth failure, not a config error."

The fail mode of the whole mechanism is silence, which is what a port to another
runtime discovers last. `feedback_gaze_external_seats_fail_open`: reviewer seats
authenticated on nothing through five runs without anything going red.

## The shape of the target

A resolver invoked at the point of use: a program taking a provider and a
variable name and writing the value to stdout. Portable by construction, since
every runtime can exec a program; it removes residency, makes 0939's trace
channel moot, and dissolves 0360 because there is no longer a cwd-dependent
selection layer to disagree about.

**This is not a design to invent — it already exists and is tested.** Ticket
0393 built exactly this for reviewer seats: `skills/reviewers/reviewers.sh`
`_keystore_file_for` + a one-variable extraction in an `env -i` subshell, with
the value never printed, logged, or placed on argv. `tests/test_reviewers.sh`
covers it with 18 sentinel-based cases including env-over-keystore precedence
and leak assertions. The work here is to promote that consumer-side pattern to
the remaining consumers and then remove the eager export, not to design a new
mechanism.

An `apiKeyHelper` (the Claude Code settings hook) is a DIFFERENT and much
narrower thing: it authenticates the client itself to one provider. It is not
the general mechanism and does not serve OpenRouter, the reviewer OpenAI
endpoint, or HAL. If ever needed it is a three-line adapter over the resolver.

## Partition

The materialization constraint — consumers needing the value at process
creation rather than at call time — was surveyed 2026-09-16 and collapses to
nearly nothing:

- `scripts/seat-runner.sh` (podman `-e VAR` bare form): ALREADY on-demand via
  0393. No work.
- `scripts/setup-claude-agent.sh` (systemd EnvironmentFile): deleted in the
  0939 PR, dead code since 0882.
- R2R (container env baked at creation): a different repo, dormant, out of scope.

So no general `with-secrets <provider> -- <cmd>` wrapper is needed. An earlier
draft of this plan proposed one; the survey removed its justification.

Children, each sized to one sign-off unit:

- 0943 — `peer_review.py`: replace `os.environ` + .env-walk with keystore resolution
- 0944 — `update-publist`: resolve HAL_ID / HAL_PASSWORD at point of use
- 0945 — `bash-env.sh`: stop exporting credentials, once 0943 and 0944 have landed

0945 is `Blocked-by` its two real prerequisites, not by this tracker.

Related, not children: 0940 (Python test hermeticity) is independent and lands
on its own schedule; 0360 (project KEYS precedence) should be closed by 0945
rather than fixed separately, and that claim must be verified at 0945's
integration review, not assumed here.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] 0943, 0944, 0945 all merged and closed
- [ ] No credential is exported by `bash-env.sh` into subprocess environments
- [ ] `bash -x -c ':'` exposes no credential value (names-only probe, as in 0939)
- [ ] Each migrated consumer has a fake-sentinel test; no test uses a real key
- [ ] 0360 re-read against the result and closed, or re-scoped with a reason
- [ ] Integration review: child diffs re-read, full suite run, not closed on the
      bare event of the last child merging

## Note 2026-09-16: credential copies outside the keystore

`~/.claude/.env` states "Rotate in the keystore only -- there is no second copy
to chase." Measured on padme, that is false in at least two places:

- `~/.config/keys/openrouter.env.bak-20260916T113037` -- a same-day backup
  holding the previous value.
- `~/.codex/auth.json` -- Codex persists its own `OPENAI_API_KEY` at rest,
  beside an OAuth token set and a `last_refresh` stamp. The harness keystore's
  `openai.env` is therefore not the only copy of that credential on this host.

This bears on portability directly: a second runtime does not just need a way to
READ the keystore, it arrives with a credential store of its own and its own
lifecycle (Codex's is a login flow writing a file, not a helper invoked at need).
A resolver does not unify those by itself. Whatever 0945 lands, the claim in the
`.env` header must be made true again or rewritten to name the exceptions.

Operator-side and out of any diff: rotating a credential must cover every copy,
not just the keystore file.

## Note 2026-09-16: two items left behind, author's call

- `scripts/projects.json` -- the registry read only by the deleted
  `setup-claude-agent.sh --list`. Zero readers remain anywhere in the repo
  (checked both spellings, the filename and the PROJECTS_JSON override). It
  describes the set of projects this harness manages, so it may be worth
  keeping as data even with no code reading it. Not deleted as collateral
  of 0941.
- `~/.config/keys/openrouter.env` holds five `EXPIRED_OPENROUTER_API_KEY_*`
  variables at rest (CIRED_DIGITAL, CLAUDE, IDH, KIEU, KILOCODE). Lower
  severity than a live key, but they are credential material kept in the
  keystore, and whether each is genuinely revoked cannot be verified from
  inside a session. The `openrouter.env.bak-20260916T113037` copy noted
  above was deleted 2026-09-16, after confirming it held no variable absent
  from the current file.

Decision recorded 2026-09-16: 0945 removes `KEYS=` outright -- no inert
no-op, no deprecation shim.
